<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="40096" href="schedule/2006/fall/CS/498/40096.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2006" href="schedule/2006.xml">2006</calendarYear><term id="120068" href="schedule/2006/fall.xml">Fall 2006</term><subject id="CS" href="schedule/2006/fall/CS.xml">Computer Science</subject><course id="498" href="schedule/2006/fall/CS/498.xml">Special Topics in CS</course></parents><sectionNumber>DP4</sectionNumber><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Topic: Program Optimization:  Prerequisites: CS 232 and CS 225.  The course will cover techniques to improve program execution speed and energy consumption. The objective is to prepare students to program future systems where performance improvements will not be, as it was in the past, the direct result of  faster clock rates, but must instead be laboriously obtained by  applying programming techniques that effectively exploit parallelism and locality. This section is for graduate students only.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Graduate - Urbana-Champaign. </sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2006-08-23Z</startDate><endDate>2006-12-08Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="L3 ">Lecture</type><start>11:00 AM</start><end>12:15 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>WF     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>1131</roomNumber><buildingName>Siebel Center for Comp Sci</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Garzaran" firstName="M">Garzaran, M</instructor><instructor lastName="Padua" firstName="D">Padua, D</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>